Wagtail Child Reorder Test Steps

Goal
Verify that children of any On Site page and any User Device page can be reordered as sibling pages in Wagtail.
Primary target requested: http://127.0.0.1:8000/cms/pages/5/

Prerequisites
1. Activate environment:
   source ~/MIP/venv/bin/activate
2. Start server:
   python manage.py runserver
3. Log in to Wagtail admin with a user that can edit/move pages.

A) Validate on the requested page (User Device page id 5)
1. Open:
   http://127.0.0.1:8000/cms/pages/5/
2. Confirm this is a User Device page and has at least two child pages (dummy slide pages are fine).
3. If there are fewer than two children, create two child pages under this parent.
4. Reorder children:
   - First make sure ordering is by manual order (ord) in the page listing (not by latest revision or title).
   - If drag handles are visible in this listing, drag one child above/below the other.
   - If drag handles are not visible in your Wagtail UI/version, use the page Move action and move one child relative to its sibling under the same parent.
5. Refresh the same URL.
6. Confirm the order is persisted.

B) Validate on another User Device page
1. Open another User Device parent page listing in Wagtail.
2. Ensure two child pages exist.
3. Reorder siblings.
4. Refresh and confirm persisted order.

C) Validate on an On Site page
1. Open an On Site parent page listing in Wagtail.
2. Ensure two child pages exist.
3. Reorder siblings.
4. Refresh and confirm persisted order.

D) Validate piece order inside Pieces
1. Open the Pieces parent page listing in Wagtail (the parent that contains Piece pages).
2. Ensure there are at least two Piece child pages.
3. Confirm listing is using manual order (ord).
4. Reorder Piece siblings:
   - If drag handles are visible, drag one Piece above/below the other.
   - If drag handles are not visible, use Move action to reposition one Piece relative to its sibling under the same Pieces parent.
5. Refresh and confirm persisted Piece order.

E) Negative checks (should NOT happen)
1. No PermissionDenied when reordering children.
2. No server errors during reorder.
3. Reorder should not require changing models.
4. If ordering is not set to manual order (ord), visible order can differ from tree order.

Useful quick checks
1. Confirm children type in models:
   - ExhibitionOnSitePage and ExhibitionUserDevicePage allow SlideshowSlidePage children.
   - PieceOnSitePage and PieceUserDevicePage allow SlideshowSlidePage children.
2. Creation order in views is only default insertion order; it does not lock future reorder.

Pass criteria
1. You can change sibling order under User Device and On Site parents.
2. You can change sibling order for Piece pages under the Pieces parent.
3. The changed order persists after page refresh.
4. The same behavior works for Exhibition and Piece branches.
